  "not_comparable": "None of these is a merchant risk feature and no number above should be read as one. A merchant risk feature is a statistic over a seller's own transaction history: its chargeback rate, its dispute rate, the share of its volume that is card-not-present. Those are computed over a merchant identifier and this file has none, so the feature cannot be built here at any strength. Published fraud results that include merchant risk are therefore not comparable with anything in this repo, in either direction, and the gap is a property of the dataset rather than of the pipeline. ADR 0019",
